{"parentUuid":"a0d64b8e-fa8c-429b-8a78-5484d27b39ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli/docs/prompts/cli-export-surface.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli/docs/prompts/cli-export-surface.md","content":"\nThe Entire CLI captures rich session and checkpoint data, but external consumers\n— Baton (issue entireio/cli#1125), eval pipelines, the in-repo\n`session-handoff` skill — currently parse internal storage directly: the\n`.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` state files for live sessions, and the v2\ncheckpoint refs for committed work. That is exactly the brittle integration\nboundary issue #1125 is asking us to replace, and the same coupling that the\n`session-handoff` skill works around today.\n\nMost of what these consumers need is already built. What is missing is the thin\nCLI surface that exposes it as a stable, supported contract:\n\n- `entire session info <id> --json` and `entire session current --json` already\n  return rich metadata (agent, model, status, worktree path, timestamps, turns,\n  checkpoints, last prompt, files touched) but cannot stream the live\n  transcript content. The handoff skill compensates by reading\n  `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` to recover `transcript_path` and grepping\n  the agent's on-disk JSONL.\n- `entire checkpoint explain` is prose-formatted only. There is no `--json`\n  output, and `--full` renders the transcript for humans rather than emitting\n  the normalized compact JSONL bytes.\n- v2 checkpoints already store both a cross-agent normalized transcript on\n  `/main` (built by `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/`) and the raw\n  per-agent transcript on `/full/*`, with readers\n  `V2GitStore.ReadSessionCompactTranscript` and `V2GitStore.ReadSessionContent`\n  ready to wrap. No new storage, no new schema is needed.\n- Within a single checkpoint that has multiple sessions (`0/`, `1/`, `2/`),\n  there is no per-session selector for transcript output today. `--session`\n  on `explain` filters the *list view* by session-ID prefix, which is a\n  different behavior.\n\nThe plan should produce small, additive CLI changes. No new top-level\ncommands, no schema invention. Treat the JSON outputs as metadata-only;\ntranscript bytes always stream to stdout from a flag, never embedded in JSON\nenvelopes (multi-MB transcripts in JSON fight `jq`, pipes, and tooling).\n\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}},"displayPath":"docs/prompts/cli-export-surface.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9269c4dc-0478-441c-ae7f-f9e0ee55a7a4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T00:05:12.840Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli","sessionId":"b3179a8b-1600-460b-a2e3-d256f3557add","version":"2.1.132","gitBranch":"checkpoint-export-cli"}
