tes files.\n35\t\n36\t  ### Worktrees\n37\t  - Default: `marvin wt new <branch-name>` — creates a worktree under\n38\t    `~/.marvin/worktrees/<repo>/<branch>` with a fresh branch off the\n39\t  current\n40\t    base. Supersedes the `~/Projects/wt` default for any new worktree work.\n41\t  - `marvin wt list` — show current worktrees (defaults to current repo).\n42\t  - `marvin wt go <name>` — print the absolute path; use as\n43\t    `cd $(marvin wt go <name>)`.\n44\t  - `marvin wt rm <name>` — remove the worktree and its branch when done.\n45\t  - Use raw `git worktree add ~/Projects/wt/...` only when explicitly\n46\t  asked.\n47\t  - Multi-repo change set: create one `marvin wt new <branch>` per repo and\n48\t    move staged work into the worktrees so main checkouts stay clean.\n49\t\n50\t  ### Memory (cross-session)\n51\t  - `marvin memory search --topic \"<keywords>\" --json` — find prior\n52\t    decisions before re-litigating them. Check this before drafting plans\n53\t    that may have been considered before.\n54\t  - `marvin memory list` / `marvin memory show <id>` — browse prior\n55\t  entries.\n56\t  - `marvin memory record-decision --title \"...\" --rationale \"...\"` —\n57\t    capture a sub-decision reached mid-task so a future session can find\n58\t  it.\n59\t  - `marvin memory record-fix --pr <num>` — capture a Pattern → Fix → File\n60\t    triple from a merged PR.\n61\t  - Memory is per-repo by default; pass `--scope global` for cross-repo\n62\t    entries. `MARVIN_MEMORY=off` skips memory for one process."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cde0cd42-8761-4631-ae27-fe3391504e3d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T01:07:00.666Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli","sessionId":"b3179a8b-1600-460b-a2e3-d256f3557add","version":"2.1.132","gitBranch":"checkpoint-export-cli"}
