mmand start; partial trailing line possible if agent is mid-\n  write\"), or scan back to the last newline before EOF and trim. The latter is\n  more robust.\n  • Confidence: 0.65 (depends on agent write buffering, which varies by\n  integration).\n\n  ### Finding D:  resolveSessionIndex  conflates \"checkpoint missing\" with\n  \"checkpoint empty\"\n\n  When  summary != nil && len(summary.Sessions) == 0 , the function returns\n   (0, ErrCheckpointNotFound) . But the checkpoint was found — it just has no\n  sessions. Callers using  errors.Is(err, ErrCheckpointNotFound)  to drive UX\n  (e.g., \"did you mistype the ID?\") will give wrong guidance.\n\n  • File/line:  explain_export.go:230-232\n  • Likely impact: confusing error UX for legitimate empty-checkpoint edge\n  case; wrong fallback in upstream callers that branch on the sentinel.\n  • Fix: return a distinct error (e.g., a new  ErrCheckpointHasNoSessions  or\n  just  errors.New(\"checkpoint has no sessions\")  — losing the sentinel here\n  is fine because no caller currently branches on it for this code path).\n  • Confidence: 0.7\n\n  ### Finding E: Path-traversal nolint annotation overstates validation\n\n   openSessionTranscript = func(path string) { return os.Open(path) }  is\n  annotated  //nolint:gosec // path is resolved from validated session state .\n  But  state.TranscriptPath  is just deserialized from  .git/entire-\n  sessions/<id>.json  — there is no validation that it's confined to any\n  directory or that it doesn't traverse symlinks. The realistic threat model\n  is low (local user already has filesystem access), but the comment is wrong,\n  and a future reader will trust it.\n\n  • File/line:  sessions.go:852-854\n  • Likely impact: documentation drift hides assumptions; if Entire ever gains\n  a daemon mode or runs under a different uid, this becomes exploitable.\n  • Fix: rewrite the comment to state the actual trust assumption (\" state.\n  TranscriptPath  is trusted because session state files are written\n  exclusively by Entire under  .git/ ; this is not validated\").\n  • Confidence: 0.6\n\n  --------\n\n  ## Top recommended fixes (in order)\n\n  1. Findings A + 1 — JSON envelope error semantics (per-session error field;\n  non-empty list path returns errors instead of  [] ). Highest user-impact bug.\n  2. Findings B + 1 — make  copySessionTranscript  ctx-aware (close-on-done\n  goroutine pattern).\n  3. Finding 4 — extract the  prefix-match + remote-fetch-on-miss  helper from\n   explain.go  and  explain_export.go . ~25 lines deduped.\n  4. Finding 5 — drop the  openSessionTranscript / copySessionTranscript\n  indirections; they are dead test infra.\n  5. Finding 6 + D — fix the misleading error message and the\n   ErrCheckpointNotFound  conflation.\n  6. Finding C — at minimum, document live-transcript snapshot semantics in  -\n  -help . Trim-to-last-newline is the better fix.\n  The rest are style/nits and can wait.\n\n\n  # codex review\n\n  Findings\n\n  1. cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go /Users/alisha/.\n  marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.\n  go:55 reimplements checkpoint resolution for the new export modes and only\n  treats  --commit  as a commit ref; the positional  target  is always handled\n  as a checkpoint prefix. That breaks the contract added in\n  cmd/entire/cli/explain.go /Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-\n  export-cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:314 that  --json  /  --transcript\n  accept a positional commit SHA, and it also skips the fetch-on-miss retry\n  path that normal explain uses in cmd/entire/cli/explain.go /Users/alisha/.\n  marvin/worktrees/cli/checkpoint-export-cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:562.\n  Result: commit-backed exports can fail even though  entire checkpoint\n  explain --commit ...  would succeed after fetching metadata. The new tests\n  only cover checkpoint IDs, not commit targets, in\n  cmd/entire/cli/explain_export_test.go /Users/alisha/.\n  marvin/worktr