metadata branch\n# ref. (Skip if you don't want to touch git state — the unit test already\n# covers this contract.)\n\n# Claude B — Ctrl-C interrupts a multi-MB stream promptly.\n# Pick a session with a large transcript and pipe to /dev/null; hit Ctrl-C.\nLARGE=$(/tmp/entire-export session list | grep \"session \" | head -1 | grep -oE 'session [a-f0-9-]+' | awk '{print $2}')\n/tmp/entire-export session info \"$LARGE\" --transcript > /dev/null\n# In another shell while it's running: kill -INT <pid>\n# Before the fix the process ran to EOF first.\n\n# Claude C — partial trailing line trimmed.\n# Easiest to fake: write a JSONL file with a truncated last record and point a\n# session at it.\ncat > /tmp/partial.jsonl <<'EOF'\n{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"complete\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"also complete\"}\n{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"trun\nEOF\n# Update a session-state file's transcript_path to /tmp/partial.jsonl then:\n/tmp/entire-export session info <id> --transcript | tail -1\n# Expect: ends with \"also complete\"} (the truncated line is dropped).\n# The unit test TestInfoCmd_TranscriptTrimsPartialTrailingLine already verifies\n# this without needing a real session.\n\n# Claude D — empty-vs-missing sentinels.\n# Covered by the unit test TestResolveSessionIndex_EmptyVsMissing; no easy\n# real-world repro since \"checkpoint with zero sessions\" is never written by\n# normal Entire flows.\n\n# Claude 6 — error message names the right flag.\n/tmp/entire-export checkpoint explain --raw-transcript 2>&1\n# Expect: \"--raw-transcript requires a checkpoint ID...\" (was \"--transcript requires...\").\n\n/tmp/entire-export checkpoint explain --transcript 2>&1\n# Expect: \"--transcript requires a checkpoint ID...\"\n\n# Claude 8 — outputMode enum. Internal refactor; no user-visible change.\n# Existing mutual-exclusion error still works:\n/tmp/entire-export session current --json --transcript 2>&1\n# Expect: cobra rejects with mutual-exclusion error.\n\n#