{"parentUuid":"b2556964-3f0d-4f4b-8aaa-699795b09a79","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fe7c94b5-a009-4688-8ac9-5ee44abd385a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RNMSwBqYBLnzxWWR73YSC","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\t[Feature Request] Support Baton-style handoff workflows from Entire session/checkpoint data\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tniketkal\nlabels:\tenhancement\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\talishakawaguchi\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1125\n--\n### Problem or use case\n\nI'm building Baton (https://github.com/niketkal/baton), a CLI-first handoff runtime for AI coding work. Baton focuses on turning in-flight work into structured, validated handoff packets for the next tool or teammate.\n\nEntire already does a different but complementary job very well:\n\ncaptures session history\npreserves prompts/transcripts\ntracks checkpoints\nsupports rewind/resume\nties work to repo/commit context\nThat makes Entire a strong source of truth for AI session capture. A useful next step would be making that captured context easier to consume in downstream handoff workflows.\n\nExample workflows where this would help:\n\nswitch from one coding tool to another mid-task\nrecover from a checkpoint and hand off cleanly\ntransfer work from agent to human or human to agent\nprepare structured context for review, eval, or automation workflows\n\n### Desired behavior\n\n```shell\nSome supported way to export Entire session/checkpoint context in a machine-readable format so downstream tools can consume it without parsing repo-internal storage directly.\n\nExample directions:\n\nentire session export --session <id> --format json\nentire checkpoint export --checkpoint <id> --format json\nentire export --all-repos --format json\nAnother possible direction would be structured JSON export from entire explain.\n\nAt minimum, downstream tooling would benefit from access to:\n\nrepo path\nsession ID\ncheckpoint ID(s)\nbranch / commit refs\ntimestamps\nprompts / transcript refs\nfiles touched\nagent / model metadata\nresume / deep-link metadata\nsummary/explain metadata if available\n```\n\n### Proposed solution\n\nI'm not suggesting that Entire adopt Baton internally or take on a Baton dependency.\n\nThe cleaner boundary seems to be exposing a supported machine-readable surface that downstream tooling can consume. Baton would be one example consumer, but the same export surface could also support:\n\ncross-repo inspection\neval tooling\nautomation\nreview tooling\nselective sharing/export workflows\n\nIf the team is already thinking about export and broader session access, this could be a good extension point for external tooling without changing Entire's core capture/recovery model.\n\n### Alternatives or workarounds\n\nThe current workaround would be for downstream tools to parse Entire's repo-internal storage directly, but that seems brittle and likely the wrong long-term integration boundary.\n\nAnother workaround is to rely on the Entire web application for visualization/sharing, but that doesn't fully address CLI-driven, machine-readable downstream tooling use cases.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5b892a6f-9f2b-4ceb-b48e-16c5c22b6575","timestamp":"2026-05-07T18:46:26.582Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"title:\t[Feature Request] Support Baton-style handoff workflows from Entire session/checkpoint data\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tniketkal\nlabels:\tenhancement\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\talishakawaguchi\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1125\n--\n### Problem or use case\n\nI'm building Baton (https://github.com/niketkal/baton), a CLI-first handoff runtime for AI coding work. Baton focuses on turning in-flight work into structured, validated handoff packets for the next tool or teammate.\n\nEntire already does a different but complementary job very well:\n\ncaptures session history\npreserves prompts/transcripts\ntracks checkpoints\nsupports rewind/resume\nties work to repo/commit context\nThat makes Entire a strong